# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# Everything in public/ is copied verbatim into out/, so this file lands at the
# root of the deployment where Pages looks for it. It costs no build step and
# no server: Pages reads it at the edge.
#
# Two rounds of restructuring, both of which moved the portfolio:
#
#   /work    the single page that carried every style before the split
#   /styles  the six collections, before they were renamed to /gallery
#
# Both have been linked from Nat's Instagram bio and indexed in between, so
# both redirect rather than 404. 301, because each move is permanent and the
# old URL should stop being served from search results.
#
# `trailingSlash: true` in next.config.ts means the canonical form of every
# route ends in a slash, hence both spellings of each.
/work           /gallery/          301
/work/          /gallery/          301
/styles         /gallery/          301
/styles/        /gallery/          301
/styles/:slug   /gallery/:slug     301
